#: docs/zh/reference/protocol/v1/index.md:24
msgid ""
"peer 严格由 `(remote_id, connection_id, session_epoch)` 标识。connection 和 epoch 的零值是普通取值，不存在短 session 回退。只有可靠"
" DATA 消耗连续的 32 位 DATA 序号；ACK、CONTROL、非可靠 DATA 的该帧头字段为零。每次签名尝试使用独立的 64 位认证序号。"
msgstr ""
"A peer is exactly `(remote_id, connection_id, session_epoch)`. Zero connection and epoch are ordinary "
"values. There is no short-session fallback. Only reliable DATA consumes the contiguous 32-bit DATA "
"sequence. ACK, CONTROL and unreliable DATA carry zero in that header field. Authentication uses a "
"separate 64-bit sequence for every signing attempt."

#: docs/zh/reference/protocol/v1/index.md:26
msgid ""
"可靠发送成功表示本地已接纳并持有数据。ACK 表示 transport 或应用已接纳，不代表写 flash 或其他业务操作已经提交。失败对该 epoch 是终态。RESET 不会将其重新开放；显式 close"
" 释放容量后，才能建立新 epoch。"
msgstr ""
"Successful reliable submission means local acceptance into owned storage. An ACK means transport or "
"application acceptance; it does not prove that flash programming or another business operation has "
"committed. Failure is terminal for an epoch. RESET cannot reopen it; explicit close releases capacity "
"before a new epoch is established."

#: docs/zh/reference/protocol/v1/index.md:28
msgid "阅读顺序"
msgstr "Reading Order"

#: docs/zh/reference/protocol/v1/index.md:30
msgid ""
"先阅读[架构](../../../explanation/architecture.md)、[线格式](wire-"
"format.md)、[扩展](extensions.md)、[可靠传输](reliability.md)和[安全](security.md)。[内存](../../../explanation/resource-"
"model.md)、[平台](../../../guides/porting.md)与[实现映射](../../../explanation/implementation-"
"map.md)说明容量、执行及源码所有权。Boot profile 使用单 peer、单包窗口；文件与固件由应用协议[分块](../../../guides/send.md)，每块单独发送。"
msgstr ""
"Read [Architecture](../../../explanation/architecture.md), [Wire Format](wire-format.md), "
"[Extensions](extensions.md), [Reliability](reliability.md) and [Security](security.md) for the principal"
" contracts. [Memory](../../../explanation/resource-model.md), [Platform](../../../guides/porting.md) and"
" [Implementation Map](../../../explanation/implementation-map.md) describe capacity, execution and "
"source ownership. The Boot profile uses one peer and a one-packet window; for files and firmware, the "
"application protocol [splits objects](../../../guides/send.md) and submits each chunk separately."
